lection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨4,4,6⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129170" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨4,8,6⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129170" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨8,4,6⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129224" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The intersection of the planes $2x-y-3z-8=0$ and $x+2y-3z-4=0$ is given by the line\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{a}_{1},{a}_{2},0⟩+tb,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2},$ and find a possible direction vector $b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129224" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We're given that there exists a point on the line where $z=0.$ Substituting this to the first equation gives\n\n$$\n2x-y-3(0)-8=0\\,⟹\\,y=2x-8,\n$$\n\nand substituting $z=0$ and $y=2x-8$ into the second equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2(2x-8)-0-4 & =0 \\\\ x+4x-16-4 & =0 \\\\ 5x & =20 \\\\ x & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=2(4)-8=0$ and $a=⟨4,0,0⟩$ is a position vector of a point on the line.\n\nNext, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $2x-y-3z-8=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨2,-1,-3⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x+2y-3z-4=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,2,-3⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨2,-1,-3⟩\\times ⟨1,2,-3⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =9i+3j+5k \\\\  & =⟨9,3,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the equation of the line is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+tb \\\\ r(t) & =⟨4,0,0⟩+t⟨9,3,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then, ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=4+0=4,$ and $b=⟨9,3,5⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129224" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b175b0ab4ad058714b06a2abaf7cc561e52cfebf3ef81caada55893e769e68f2" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129224" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129224" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=-2,\\,b=⟨6,3,5⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129224" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=-4,\\,b=⟨9,5,3⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129224" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=2,\\,b=⟨3,9,5⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129224" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=4,\\,b=⟨9,3,5⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129224" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=8,\\,b=⟨5,3,9⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The intersection of the planes $2x-y+6=0$ and $y+2z-2=0$ is given by the line\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{a}_{1},0,{a}_{3}⟩+tb,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate ${a}_{1}-{a}_{3},$ and find a possible direction vector $b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We're given that there exists a point on the line where $y=0.$ Substituting this to the first equation gives \n\n$$\n2x-0+6=0\\,⟹\\,x=-3,\n$$\n\nand substituting $y=0$ into the second equation gives\n\n$$\n0+2z-2=0\\,⟹\\,z=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=⟨-3,0,1⟩$ is a position vector of a point on the line.\n\nNext, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $2x-y+6=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨2,-1,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $y+2z-2=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,1,2⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,0⟩\\times ⟨0,1,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-2i-4j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-4,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation of the line is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+tb \\\\ r(t) & =⟨-3,0,1⟩+t⟨-2,-4,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally then, ${a}_{1}-{a}_{3}=-3-1=-4,$ and $b=⟨-2,-4,2⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b175b0ab4ad058714b06a2abaf7cc561e52cfebf3ef81caada55893e769e68f2" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71347" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71347" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{a}_{1}-{a}_{3}=-2,\\,b=⟨-4,2,2⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71347" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{a}_{1}-{a}_{3}=-4,\\,b=⟨-2,-4,2⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71347" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{a}_{1}-{a}_{3}=2,\\,b=⟨-4,2,2⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9